	"description": [
		"This course prepares McNair Scholars for the rigors of academic writing. The enrolled students represent a variety of disciplines, so this course is not meant to replace discipline-specific research methods or writing courses. Students review disciplinary scholarly literature, prepare a formal poster presentation, practice communicating their work to different audiences, explore the historical and social contexts of academic writing, and reflect on their own summer experience. Offered every summer. Prerequisite: successful completion of Writing and Rhetoric."
